 "result_text": "`__all__, = (...)` no longer crashes pyflakes. Running it on the issue's example now exits cleanly with no output, and the existing test suite passes (714 passed, 44 skipped). I didn't add a test, as instructed.\n\n`ExportBinding` was being built for any `__all__` binding at module level, including tuple unpacking. Its source was then the `Tuple` rather than an assignment, which has no `.value`. I changed `handleNodeStore` in `pyflakes/checker.py` so `ExportBinding` is only built when the name's direct parent is an `Assign`, `AugAssign` or `AnnAssign`. Other forms, such as `__all__, = ...`, now get an ordinary binding.\n\nI did not add the \"mark this as invalid\" warning the issue suggests. The unpacking form is treated as a normal binding, so its names aren't checked as exports.",
